            <ArticleTitle>Wiring of tortuous coronary arteries-let the heart do the hard work!</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>597-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tortuous coronary arteries pose a special problem for the cardiac interventionists. They are associated with difficulty in advancement of guidewire, balloons and stents across the coronaries with higher complications. We describe an interesting phenomenon of &quot;self advancement of guidewire&quot; in tortuous coronary arteries with an illustrative case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
